# TARGET ARCHITECTURE: aarch64 (ARM64) | v0.16.1 | gcp/rocky9
# ARM64-specific syscall mapping; reconcile against this product/version ARM64 STIG or approved baseline.
# Enterprise Linux Audit v0.16.1  |  [gcp/rocky9]
# Tier: tier-1-baseline
# Purpose: MAC administrative policy changes and enforcement context
# Source/authority: DISA applicable product STIG/SRG as applicable; vendor SELinux/AppArmor docs
# Architecture: aarch64 (b64 only). No x86/compat b32 syscall rules.
# Release state: engineering candidate; NOT independently certified STIG compliant.


# SELinux policy configuration; SELinux AVC denials are emitted by the subsystem itself.
-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -F dir=/etc/selinux -F perm=wa -k t1_selinux_policy
# OPTIONAL command monitors if binaries exist:
# -a always,exit -F arch=b64 -F path=/usr/sbin/semanage -F perm=x -k t1_selinux_admin
# -a always,exit -F arch=b64 -F path=/usr/sbin/setsebool -F perm=x -k t1_selinux_admin
# Enforcement mode must be checked separately with getenforce/sestatus.
